<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Vitus Bering</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1681–<a href="/years/1741">1741</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Vitus Bering was a Danish-born navigator in Russian service who led two great expeditions to the North Pacific. On the first, in 1728, he sailed through the strait between Asia and America that now bears his name; on the second he reached the coast of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alaska">Alaska</a> in 1741, but died of scurvy on the return voyage on what is now Bering Island.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/vitus-bering.jpg" alt="Vitus Bering" width="320" height="321" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Институт Археологии РАН (Institute of Archaeology in Russian Academy of Sciences) · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Vitus_Bering_reconstruction.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
